      "transcript": "Third Thursday of November. Half a million teenagers sit down for one exam, and at ten past one in the afternoon, for thirty-five minutes, the whole country goes quiet for them. Aircraft hold above three kilometres. Artillery drills stop. No horns within two hundred metres of a school.",
